From 02a065c28fbb02341161b98993f2e1157c06ff12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: minhmc2007 <quangminh21072010@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 05:35:12 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] envsetup: do not enable ccache

Two separate reasons, both of which had to be fixed.

setup_ccache exports USE_CCACHE=1 and points CCACHE_EXEC at ccache on every
envsetup, so each build wrote a cache whether or not one was wanted. It also
sets CCACHE_MAXSIZE itself, but a cache left at its default is unbounded.
Commenting out the call rather than the body leaves USE_CCACHE unset, so
USE_CCACHE=1 in the environment still works, and re-enabling is deleting one
character.

The gate in core/ccache.mk only matched the literal word false:

  ifneq ($(filter-out false,$(USE_CCACHE)),)

filter-out returns the whole list minus the words it is given, so any other
value survived, including 0, no and off. USE_CCACHE=0 therefore enabled
ccache. That matters because the two gates disagree: soong's IsEnvTrue
rejects 0, but ccache.mk is what sets CC_WRAPPER and the CCACHE_* variables
that soong then uses, and it is the permissive one.

The visible symptom was not a ccache problem at all:

  ccache: error: Not a directory

Nothing created ~/.cache/ccache once setup_ccache was disabled, and soong
passes -B ~/.cache/ccache to nsjail. nsjail's -B creates a missing bind
source as an empty regular file, so ccache was handed a file where it
wanted a directory and every compile failed at the wrapper. The dir was
replaced by hand to get the build moving; this makes the configuration
itself correct instead.

Accepting the usual falsy spellings keeps ccache re-enablable: 1, yes, true
and any other non-empty value still turn it on, so nothing is removed.

Change-Id: Ia38263cc5e06f4c2449f44bf833fd7189c8c058f
---
 core/ccache.mk | 4 +++-
 envsetup.sh    | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/ccache.mk b/core/ccache.mk
index d10aceb..eb8dcf3 100644
--- a/core/ccache.mk
+++ b/core/ccache.mk
@@ -29,7 +29,9 @@
 # So if you still want to use ccache, continue setting USE_CCACHE, but also set
 # the CCACHE_EXEC environment variable to the path to your ccache executable.
 ifneq ($(CCACHE_EXEC),)
-ifneq ($(filter-out false,$(USE_CCACHE)),)
+# filter-out matched only the literal word false, so USE_CCACHE=0 enabled ccache
+# instead of disabling it. Accept the usual falsy spellings as off.
+ifneq ($(filter-out false 0 no off,$(USE_CCACHE)),)
   # The default check uses size and modification time, causing false misses
   # since the mtime depends when the repo was checked out
   CCACHE_COMPILERCHECK ?= content
diff --git a/envsetup.sh b/envsetup.sh
index db06cb6..2bdc2ec 100644
--- a/envsetup.sh
+++ b/envsetup.sh
@@ -3496,7 +3496,8 @@ function skipGlobs() {
 }
 
 setup_keys
-setup_ccache
+# ccache off, it defaults USE_CCACHE=1 and grows without bound.
+#setup_ccache
 validate_current_shell
 set_global_paths
 source_vendorsetup
-- 
